  "script": "With its aggressive, angular front fascia, the 2025 Cadillac CT5-V Blackwing showcases a prominent black mesh grille and sharp LED headlights that hint at its performance. The V-Series badging on the front fender underscores its position as a high-performance variant within Cadillac's lineup. At the rear, the carbon fiber spoiler isn\u2019t just for looks; it enhances aerodynamic efficiency and adds to the Blackwing\u2019s sporty aesthetic. Under the hood, a supercharged 6.2-liter V8 pumps out 668 horsepower and 659 lb-ft of torque, making this beast a real powerhouse. Originally priced around $95K, the CT5-V Blackwing now holds steady at about $105K, reflecting a rare appreciation of about 2% a year. Inside, the carbon fiber trim surrounding the gear shifter highlights Cadillac\u2019s focus on performance-oriented luxury. A rarity today, the manual gear shifter with suede and metal accents connects driver and machine with a tactile feel. In the showdown with BMW\u2019s M3, the Cadillac\u2019s 668 hp beats the BMW's 473 hp. However, both clock similar quarter-mile times.",
